um</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">UBC 399MNT</span><span class=\"box-title\">UB Curriculum Capstone</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">1 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"statistics-ba__box-4-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"statistics-ba__box-4-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Regression Analysis&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Covers regression analysis and introduction to linear models. Topics include point estimation, confidence intervals, hypothesis testing, simple linear regression, multiple regression, analysis of covariance, and non-linear regression. The course uses statistical software and emphasizes hands-on applications to data sets from a variety of settings.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: STA 301 /STA 301 and STA 302 /STA 302&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">STA 403LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Regression Analysis</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></